    "methodology_summary": "The authors develop a theoretical two-factor asset pricing model incorporating market risk and an endogenous diversification/internal consistency risk factor resulting from the heavy-tailed distribution of firm sizes. They test the model using monthly excess returns on 25 size- and book-to-market-sorted portfolios as well as industry portfolios from January 1927 to December 2005. Regressions and bootstrap confidence intervals are used to compare the explanatory power of this two-factor model against the standard Fama-French three-factor model.",
